Spec: Authenticated Java peer stream client

Purpose:
  Attach a device and application scoped business stream to an authorized publishing Agent.

Owns:
  ./PeerClient.java

References:
  ./DeviceIdentity.sdd
  ./BusinessChannel.sdd
  /windows/LinkGate.Broker/SecurePeerServer.sdd

Must:
  Use the same eight-second established-renewal budget as Windows for both socket reads and the raw-socket cancellation timer, without extending opening or signed lease expiry.
  Authenticate both independent channels to the expected device before delivering business bytes.
  Use an explicit bounded endpoint and one total opening deadline, never retry payload or replace peer identity.
  Validate one-use attachment and grant responses and keep control renewals independent of blocked business IO.
  Preserve fixed authenticated peer refusals as authorization/capacity outcomes rather than reporting them as offline transport failures.
  Close all owned resources after control loss, cancellation, certificate expiry or failed setup.
  Accept an optional Agent-owned lease source for a distinct server-authorized wire shape; require a bounded token on open and every heartbeat and never retry without it.
  Run lease refresh on the bounded control executor under the existing heartbeat cancellation deadline, preserving raw-socket abort behavior.
  Accept a remaining internal opening budget of one to sixty thousand milliseconds so earlier server authorization and runtime preparation do not reset the application's total deadline.
